    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the Python file that generates an embedding vector for a text string using a concrete external provider, I will use the Hugging Face Transformers library, which is a popular choice for natural language processing tasks. This library provides access to various pre-trained models, including those for generating embeddings. I will import the necessary components from the transformers library and use a specific model identifier to make the provider identifiable in the code. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789887581947,
          "start": 1789887579074
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
